      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-05T22:10:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not 100% sure, since I wouldn\u0027t expect the `Device()` constructor to run if `new` failed, but calling `registerDevice` from inside the constructor was one hypothesis for the crash reports in b/333073673.\n\nEven if that\u0027s not the case, this feels better because now we don\u0027t expose the device pointer to anything until it\u0027s been put into an `sk_sp`.",
